by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-02T08:29:00Z

The comparison that matters here is not `#[AsMessage]` but Validator and Serializer metadata, which indeed work on any class without discovery. Those answer a different question though: "given this object in hand, what are its rules", so lazy runtime reading fits them. A form type is resolved by name before any object exists: `createForm(UserDto::class)` looks up a named service in the type registry, next to the other types, extensions and guessers, which are all container services. This feature derives such a service from the class, and deriving services is what the container does. It is also what enables `new Reference(...)` in options and `extendedBy`; a runtime metadata reader cannot inject services.

In practice the requirement is: the class lives under `src/` like every other class of the app, which is the default everywhere. Closing the topic on my side.

